From: XR1710G Community <xr1710g-community@localhost>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 02:36:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: NPU: evaluate HIT_UNBIND packets for PPE offload

Mirror the Airoha Ethernet-side unbind handling on the MT7996 NPU RX path.
Mesh bridge traffic can stay in PPE UNBIND state without producing the rate
threshold reason, preventing airoha_ppe_dev_check_skb() from ever preparing
the reverse Wi-Fi-to-wired hardware path.

Evaluate both HIT_UNBIND and HIT_UNBIND_RATE_REACHED. Bound flows leave this
path automatically; flows that cannot be offloaded continue through the
normal software datapath.

---
 npu.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/npu.c
+++ b/npu.c
@@ -417,7 +417,8 @@ void mt76_npu_check_ppe(struct mt76_dev
 	skb_set_hash(skb, hash, PKT_HASH_TYPE_L4);
 
 	reason = FIELD_GET(NPU_RX_DMA_CRSN_MASK, info);
-	if (reason == PPE_CPU_REASON_HIT_UNBIND_RATE_REACHED) {
+	if (reason == PPE_CPU_REASON_HIT_UNBIND ||
+	    reason == PPE_CPU_REASON_HIT_UNBIND_RATE_REACHED) {
 		skb_set_mac_header(skb, 0);
 		airoha_ppe_dev_check_skb(ppe_dev, skb, hash, true);
 	}
